        <a href="/match/" data-match-open>Tell us your situation and get a shortlist of advisors →</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ═══ 3. COMPARE — the details that change what you pay ═══ -->
  <section class="section section--alt" id="compare">
    <div class="container">
      <header class="sec-head">
        <p class="kicker">Side by side</p>
        <h2 class="sec-title">The details that change what you pay</h2>
        <p class="sec-desc">
          Scores, prices and terms come from our platform reviews (re-checked {lastChecked}) and the
          {siteStats.total} advisor profiles we’ve audited — not from the platforms’ marketing pages.
        </p>
      </header>

      <div class="cmp-wrap">
        <table class="cmp">
          <caption class="sr-only">Kasamba, Purple Garden and Keen compared</caption>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th scope="col" class="cmp-corner"><span class="sr-only">Feature</span></th>
              {platforms.map((p, i) => (
                <th scope="col" class:list={['cmp-plat', { 'cmp-plat--top': i === 0 }]}>
                  <img src={p.logo} alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy" />
                  <span>{p.name}</span>
                  {i === 0 && <span class="cmp-badge">Our #1</span>}
                </th>
              ))}
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            {compareRows.map((row) => (
              <tr>
                <th scope="row">
                  {row.label}
                  {row.hint && <span class="cmp-hint" set:html={row.hint} />}
                </th>
                {platforms.map((p, i) => (
                  <td data-label={p.name} class:list={{ 'cmp-top': i === 0 }}><span class="cmp-v" set:html={row.value(p)} /></td>
                ))}
              </tr>
            ))}
          </tbody>
          <tfoot>
            <tr>
              <th scope="row"><span class="sr-only">Visit</span></th>
              {platforms.map((p) => (
                <td data-label={p.name}>
                  <a href={p.affiliateUrl} class="btn btn--primary btn--sm btn--full" rel="nofollow sponsored" target="_blank" data-cta-source="home-table">{p.ctaLabel}</a>
                </td>
              ))}
            </tr>
          </tfoot>
        </table>
      </div>

      <p class="cmp-more">
        Deciding between two?
        <a href="/comparisons/kasamba-vs-keen/">Kasamba vs Keen</a> ·
        <a href="/comparisons/purple-garden-vs-kasamba/">Purple Garden vs Kasamba</a> ·
        <a href="/comparisons/purple-garden-vs-keen/">Purple Garden vs Keen</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ═══ 3b. OUR DATA — original, citable numbers from the audits ═══ -->
  <section class="section" id="data">
    <div class="container">
      <header class="sec-head">
        <p class="kicker">Original data</p>
        <h2 class="sec-title">What {siteStats.total} advisor audits show</h2>
        <p class="sec-desc">
          Every advisor we audit gets a recorded listed rate and a 1–5 audit score. These figures are
          recalculated from those audits whenever they change. Last updated
          <time datetime={auditStats.lastUpdated}>{auditMonthYear}</time>.
        </p>
      </header>

      <ul class="stats" aria-label="Headline numbers from our advisor audits">
        <li class="stat">
          <strong>{ov.profiles}</strong>
          <span>advisor profiles audited across {auditRows.length} platforms</span>
        </li>
        <li class="stat">
          <strong>{money(ov.medianListedRate)}<small>/min</small></strong>
          <span>median listed rate, lowest to highest {money(ov.lowestListedRate)}–{money(ov.highestListedRate)}</span>
        </li>
        <li class="stat">
          <strong>{ov.shareAtOrUnder5PerMin}<small>%</small></strong>
          <span>of advisors list $5.00/min or less</span>
        </li>
        <li class="stat">
          <strong>{ov.averageAuditScore.toFixed(2)}<small>/5</small></strong>
          <span>average audit score; 80% of advisors score {ov.auditScoreP10.toFixed(1)}–{ov.auditScoreP90.toFixed(1)}, so <em>fit</em> matters more than rating</span>
        </li>
      </ul>

      <div class="cmp-wrap">
        <table class="cmp data-table">
          <caption class="sr-only">Listed rates and audit scores by platform</caption>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th scope="col">Platform</th>
              <th scope="col">Profiles audited</th>
              <th scope="col">Median listed rate</th>
              <th scope="col">Lowest – highest</th>
              <th scope="col">At or under $5/min</th>
              <th scope="col">Average audit score</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            {auditRows.map((r) => (
              <tr>
                <th scope="row"><a href={`/reviews/${r.key}/`}>{r.name}</a></th>
                <td data-label="Profiles audited">{r.profiles}</td>
                <td data-label="Median listed rate">{money(r.medianListedRate)}/min</td>
                <td data-label="Lowest – highest">{money(r.lowestListedRate)} – {money(r.highestListedRate)}</td>
                <td data-label="At or under $5/min">{r.shareAtOrUnder5PerMin}%</td>
                <td data-label="Average audit score">{r.averageAuditScore.toFixed(2)}</td>
              </tr>
            ))}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <p class="data-note">
        {spreadSentence} A “listed rate” is the lowest per-minute rate on an advisor’s public profile; advisors
        set and change their own prices, so confirm the rate on the profile before you book.
        Method: <a href="/methodology/">how we audit and score</a>.
        Free to quote with a link to this page. Raw numbers:
        <a href="/data/psychic-platform-audit.json">psychic-platform-audit.json</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ═══ 4. BEFORE YOU PAY — fine print + red flags ═══ -->
  <section class="section" id="before-you-pay">
    <div class="container">
      <header class="sec-head">
        <p class="kicker">Avoid the traps</p>
        <h2 class="sec-title">Read this before you claim any offer</h2>
        <p class="sec-desc">
          Every welcome offer has a catch. None of them are deal-breakers — as long as you know them going in.
        </p>
      </header>

      <div class="playbook">
        {platforms.map((p) => (
          <article class="pb">
            <h3 class="pb-title">
              <img src={p.logo} alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy" />
              <span>{p.name}<small>{p.offer}</small></span>
            </h3>
            <p class="pb-label pb-label--catch">The catch</p>
            <ul class="pb-list">
              {p.catches.map((c) => <li>{c}</li>)}
            </ul>
            <p class="pb-label pb-label--play">Play it like this</p>
            <p class="pb-play">{p.play}</p>
          </article>
        ))}
      </div>

      <div class="flags">
        <div class="flags-head">
          <h3 class="flags-title">Walk away from any reader, on any platform, who gives you…</h3>
          <a href="/guides/how-to-spot-fake-psychic/" class="flags-link">All 13 red flags →</a>
        </div>
        <ol class="flags-list">
          {redFlags.map((f) => (
            <li><strong>{f.title}</strong> {f.body}</li>
          ))}
        </ol>
        <p class="flags-foot">
          Also worth ten minutes before your first session:
          <a href="/guides/before-you-pay-for-a-psychic-reading/">13 things to know before you pay</a> ·
          <a href="/guides/questions-to-ask-a-psychic/">Questions that get real answers</a> ·
          <a href="/guides/free-psychic-readings-online-truth/">What “free reading” really means</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ═══ 5. SITUATIONS — route by intent + the matching tool ═══ -->
  <section class="section section--alt" id="situations">
    <div class="container">
      <header class="sec-head">
        <p class="kicker">Start from your situation</p>
        <h2 class="sec-title">What are you trying to find out?</h2>
        <p class="sec-desc">Each guide names the advisors we’d book for that exact question — and the ones we wouldn’t.</p>
