              <div><dt>Our score</dt><dd>{r.rating}/5</dd></div>
              <div><dt>Listed rate</dt><dd>{money(r.rate as number)}/min</dd></div>
            </dl>
            {r.proof && <p class="adv-proof">{r.proof}</p>}
            {r.bestFor && <p class="adv-for"><strong>Best for:</strong> {shorten(r.bestFor)}</p>}
            <div class="adv-actions">
              <a href={r.affiliateUrl} class="btn btn--primary btn--sm" rel="nofollow sponsored" target="_blank" data-cta-source="home-advisor">See profile on {r.platformName} →</a>
              <a href={r.url} class="adv-audit">Read our audit</a>
            </div>
          </article>
        ))}
      </div>

      <p class="advisors-foot">
        Browse every audited advisor:
        {platforms.map((p, i) => (
          <>{i > 0 && ' · '}<a href={p.reviewUrl}>{p.name} ({p.profiles})</a></>
        ))}
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ═══ 7. TRUST — how we test, what we refuse to do, who we are ═══ -->
  <section class="section section--alt" id="method">
    <div class="container">
      <header class="sec-head">
        <p class="kicker">How we test</p>
        <h2 class="sec-title">Why these verdicts hold up</h2>
      </header>

      <div class="trust">
        <ol class="steps">
          <li>
            <h3>Normal accounts, our own money</h3>
            <p>No press accounts or sponsored credit — only the welcome offer any new client gets.</p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <h3>Several readers, one question framework</h3>
            <p>We never judge a platform on one advisor, and we ask everyone the same kind of question so answers are comparable.</p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <h3>Predictions logged — then checked</h3>
            <p>Dated predictions go in a ledger and get re-checked when the window passes. Public track records get audited the same way.</p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <h3>Fixed, published weights</h3>
            <p>Scoring weights are set before testing and <a href="/methodology/#scoring-framework">published in full</a>. No platform can negotiate them.</p>
          </li>
        </ol>

        <div class="wont">
          <h3 class="wont-title">What we won’t do</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Sell a ranking, a badge or a “featured” slot.</li>
            <li>Put a percentage on psychic accuracy. “87% accurate” is unverifiable — we score how specific and checkable a reading is instead.</li>
            <li>Recommend anyone who uses fear tactics. One strike, whatever their rating.</li>
            <li>Rank an advisor we haven’t audited.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <figure class="author">
        <img src="/sarah-avatar.jpg" alt="Sarah, founder of Eastern Alignment" width="72" height="72" loading="lazy" />
        <figcaption>
          <p class="author-quote">
            “I’ve studied astrology, tarot, BaZi and feng shui since I was 21, and I’ve spent the last three years
            booking online readings as an ordinary paying customer. I built this site because I couldn’t find one
            that told me the truth <em>before</em> I spent the money.”
          </p>
          <p class="author-meta">
            <strong>Sarah</strong>, founder ·
            <a href="/about/">My story</a> · <a href="/methodology/">Full methodology</a> · <a href="/disclosure/">How we’re funded</a>
          </p>
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ═══ 8. FAQ ═══ -->
  <section class="section home-faq">
    <div class="container container--narrow">
      <FAQ items={homeFAQs} title="Before you book: common questions" />
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

